      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've test that on some SDK versions, and here is result:\n\n3.5.0 : Reproduced\n\n3.5.1 : Reproduced\n\n3.5.2 : Reproduced Unless VRCObjectSync GameObject is enabled\n\n3.6.0 : Reproduced\n\n3.6.1 : Reproduced\n\n3.7.0 : Reproduced\n\n3.7.1 : Reproduced\n\n3.7.2 : Reproduced\n\n3.7.3 : Reproduced\n\n3.7.4 : Reproduced\n\n3.7.5 : Reproduced\n\nand here is code:\n\nusing VRC.SDK3.Components;\n\npublic class SetGravityKinematicTest : UdonSharpBehaviour\n\n{\n\n    public VRCObjectSync sync;  // set your disabled VRCObjectSync thing\n\n    public override void Interact()\n\n    {\n\n        sync.SetGravity(true);\n\n        sync.SetKinematic(false);\n\n    }\n\n}\n\nI wonder if VRCObjectSync gets that's own Rigidbody in Start(), but disabled VRCObjectSync dont have it, so causes exception.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
